/-! # Primitive generation from zero Verschiebung

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Proposition 14.48, printed pp. 295–296,
and Definition 14.45, printed p. 295
(blueprint: lem-sfb-zero-verschiebung-primitive-generation).

Vanishing refers to the canonical coordinate construction of Verschiebung, including
on nonreduced schemes. Generation is expressed by a finite polynomial for every function.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TensorProduct

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AffineGroupFrobeniusVerschiebung

/-- Zero canonical Verschiebung implies that every coordinate function is a polynomial
over the base field in finitely many primitive coordinate functions.
Source: Milne, Proposition 14.48 and Definition 14.45, printed pp. 295–296
(blueprint: lem-sfb-zero-verschiebung-primitive-generation).

Proof plan:
1. Write the primitive subspace as the kernel of the reduced coproduct. A basis expansion
   of any field extension shows that this kernel commutes with scalar extension, using
   lem-sfb-affine-group-coordinate-hopf and the tensor pushout universal property.
2. Extend to an algebraic closure. By lem-sfb-verschiebung-naturality-diagonalizable,
   zero Verschiebung persists and excludes nontrivial diagonalizable closed subgroups:
   their Verschiebung is both zero and an isomorphism, forcing them to be trivial.
3. Apply lem-sfb-commutative-no-diagonalizable-additive-filtration. Induct on its finite
   chain, starting with the trivial group embedded in the zero-dimensional vector group.
4. At each step push out the extension along each additive coordinate of the previous
   embedding, by lem-sfb-affine-commutative-extension-pushout. Verschiebung of the pushout
   vanishes by the product and quotient clauses of the naturality lemma and the additive
   formula of lem-sfb-length-two-witt-extension-verschiebung.
5. Over the perfect algebraic closure, lem-sfb-additive-subgroup-commutative-extensions-witt
   presents each pushout as the pullback of the length-two Witt extension along h.
   Naturality and the Witt Verschiebung formula give (h q') twisted by Frobenius equal
   to zero. Invert the scalar twist, then cancel the fppf epimorphism q', obtaining h=0.
   This concerns morphisms, so it remains valid on nonreduced schemes.
6. The zero pullback splits. Its additive retraction extends the chosen coordinate of
   the subgroup. Combine all these extensions, including the empty family in dimension zero.
7. Append the coordinate of the additive quotient. The resulting homomorphism has trivial
   scheme-theoretic kernel on every algebra-valued point. The theorem
   lem-sfb-algebraic-group-homomorphism-factorization then makes it a closed embedding.
8. Its surjective coordinate map from a polynomial algebra yields primitive generators,
   by the affine closed-immersion criterion and the coproduct of def-sc-gm-ga.
9. Let A be the subalgebra generated by the original primitives. Step 1 and generation
   after extension imply that every 1 tensor c lies in the image of K tensor A. Choose
   a k-linear retraction K to k sending 1 to 1 and apply it to this finite tensor sum.
   This proves c belongs to A, equivalently the finite polynomial expression below.
No smoothness, connectedness, reducedness, or perfection of the original field is used. -/
theorem zero_verschiebung_primitive_generation
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP k p]
    (G : Scheme.{u}) [G.Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))] [IsAffine G]
    [GrpObj (G.asOver (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)))]
    [IsCommMonObj (G.asOver (Spec (CommRingCat.of k)))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (G ↘ Spec (CommRingCat.of k))]
    [QuasiCompact (G ↘ Spec (CommRingCat.of k))]
    (hV : ∀ c : Γ(G, ⊤),
      projection k p Γ(G, ⊤) (iteratedComul k Γ(G, ⊤) p c) =
        algebraMap k (twist k p Γ(G, ⊤)) (Coalgebra.counit (R := k) c)) :
    ∀ c : Γ(G, ⊤), ∃ (n : ℕ) (x : Fin n → Γ(G, ⊤)) (f : MvPolynomial (Fin n) k),
      (∀ i : Fin n, Coalgebra.comul (R := k) (x i) =
        x i ⊗ₜ[k] (1 : Γ(G, ⊤)) + (1 : Γ(G, ⊤)) ⊗ₜ[k] x i) ∧
      MvPolynomial.aeval x f = c := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AffineGroupFrobeniusVerschiebung
